      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The action of morphine, promedol, fentanyl and pentazocin on nociceptive transmission in the spinal cord was studied in unanesthetized spinal rats with the use of intraarterial injection of bradykinin. When used in the same doses, the opiates also reduced the firing of the axons of the ascending portions of the spinal cord. Naloxon rapidly antagonized the action of the narcotics."},
